-- Setting: DuckDB v1.5.6 (069cc9f9b5) with spatial 04270fe and Flock b719767d from the community
-- repository; Ollama 0.24.0 (ollama serve with OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH=8192) serving llama3
-- (368f4f3f44d0) and gpt-oss:20b (a0b38d0b19f7) on an NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 Laptop GPU;
-- flock_pipelines.sql of this directory ("max_batch_size": 1 in both CREATE MODEL statements,
-- "think": "low" for gpt-oss), over the Parquet files that export_tables.sql writes from the
-- Hanoi database of load/hanoi_duckdb_csv.sql.
-- Why Ollama 0.24.0: from 0.30.0 Ollama runs models through llama-server and starts it with
-- --embedding only for models whose metadata has pooling_type, so it refuses the llama3
-- embeddings of pipeline5 ('This server does not support embeddings'); 0.24.0 returns llama3's
-- 4096-dimension embedding. The Ollama registry refuses gpt-oss:20b to a 0.24.0 client ("requires
-- a newer version of Ollama"), so a newer client downloads it once; 0.24.0 serves it.
